4.308 Contract closeout

L1:(a) The administrative closeout procedures must ensure that—
L2:(1) Disposition of classified material is completed;
L2:(2) Final patent report is cleared. If a final patent report is required, the contracting officer may proceed with contract closeout according to the following procedures, or as otherwise prescribed by agency procedures:
L3:(i) Final patent reports should be cleared within 60 days of receipt.
L3:(ii) If the final patent report is not received, the contracting officer must notify the contractor of the contractor's obligations and the Government's rights under the applicable patent rights clause, according to part 27. If the contractor fails to respond to this notification, the contracting officer may proceed with contract closeout upon consultation with the agency legal counsel responsible for patent matters regarding the contractor's failure to respond.
L2:(3) Final royalty report is cleared;
L2:(4) There is no outstanding value engineering change proposal;
L2:(5) Plant clearance report is received;
L2:(6) Property clearance is received;
L2:(7) All interim or disallowed costs are settled;
L2:(8) Price revision is completed;
L2:(9) The prime contractor settles its subcontracts;
L2:(10) Prior year indirect cost rates are settled;
L2:(11) Termination docket is completed;
L2:(12) Contract audit is completed;
L2:(13) Contractor's closing statement is completed;
L2:(14) Contractor's final invoice has been submitted; and
L2:(15) Contract funds review is completed and excess funds deobligated.
L1:(b) When the actions in paragraph (a) of this section have been verified, the contracting officer administering the contract must prepare a contract completion statement containing the following information:
L2:(1) Contract administration office name and address (if different from the contracting office).
L2:(2) Contracting office name and address.
L2:(3) Contract number.
L2:(4) Last modification number.
L2:(5) Last call or order number.
L2:(6) Contractor name and address.
L2:(7) Dollar amount of excess funds, if any.
L2:(8) Voucher number and date, if final payment has been made.
L2:(9) Invoice number and date, if the final approved invoice has been forwarded to a disbursing office of another agency or activity and the status of the payment is unknown.
L2:(10) A statement that all required contract administration actions have been fully and satisfactorily accomplished.
L2:(11) Name and signature of the contracting officer.
L2:(12) Date.
L1:(c) When the statement is completed, the contracting officer must place—
L2:(1) The signed original in the contracting office contract file (or forwarded to the contracting office for placement in the files if the contract administration office is different from the contracting office); and
L2:(2) A signed copy in the appropriate contract administration file if administration is performed by a contract administration office.

