9.205 Opportunity for qualification before award

L1:(a) If an agency determines that a qualification requirement is necessary, the agency activity responsible for establishing the requirement must—
L2:(1) Urge manufacturers and other potential sources to demonstrate their ability to meet the standards specified for qualification;
L2:(2) When possible, give sufficient time to arrange for qualification before award; and
L2:(3) Before establishing any qualification requirement, furnish notice through the GPE. The notice must include—
L3:(i) A statement of the intent to establish a qualification requirement;
L3:(ii) The specification number and name of the product;
L3:(iii) The name and address of the activity to which to submit a request for the information and opportunity;
L3:(iv) The anticipated date that the agency will begin awarding contracts subject to the qualification requirement;
L3:(v) A precautionary notice that when a product is submitted for qualification testing, the applicant must furnish any specific information that may be requested of the manufacturer before testing will begin; and
L3:(vi) The approximate time period following submission of a product for qualification testing within which the applicant will be notified whether the product passed or failed the qualification testing (see 9.202(a)(5)).
L1:(b) The activity responsible for establishing a qualification requirement must keep any list maintained of those already qualified open for inclusion of additional products, manufacturers, or other potential sources.

9.207 Changes in status regarding qualification requirements

L1:(a) Promptly report to the agency activity that established the qualification requirement any conditions meriting removal or omission from a QPL, QML, or QBL or that affect whether a source should continue as identified as meeting the requirement. These conditions exist when—
L2:(1) Products or services are submitted for inspection or acceptance that do not meet the qualification requirement;
L2:(2) Products or services were previously rejected and the defects were not corrected when resubmitted for inspection or acceptance;
L2:(3) A supplier fails to request reevaluation following change of location or ownership of the plant where the product which met the qualification requirement was manufactured (see the clause at 52.209-1, Qualification Requirements);
L2:(4) A manufacturer of a product which met the qualification requirement has discontinued manufacture of the product;
L2:(5) A source requests removal from a QPL, QML, or QBL;
L2:(6) A condition of meeting the qualification requirement was violated; e.g., advertising or publicity contrary to 9.204(b)(7)(v);
L2:(7) A revised specification imposes a new qualification requirement;
L2:(8) Manufacturing or design changes have been incorporated in the qualification requirement;
L2:(9) The source is listed in the System for Award Management Exclusions (see subpart 9.4); or
L2:(10) Performance of a contract subject to a qualification requirement is otherwise unsatisfactory.
L1:(b) After considering these or other conditions related to whether a product or source continues to meet the standards specified for qualification, an agency may take appropriate action without advance notification. The agency must, however, promptly notify the affected parties if a product or source is removed from a QPL, QML, or QBL, or will no longer be identified as meeting the standards specified for qualification. This notice must contain specific information why the product or source no longer meets the qualification requirement.

9.304 Exceptions

L0:Normally, do not require testing and approval in contracts for—
L1:(a) Research or development;
