L1:(e) When the audiovisual or other special works are produced to accomplish a public purpose other than acquisition for the Government's own use (such as for production and distribution to the public of the works by other than a Federal agency) agencies are authorized to specially negotiate rights in special works that meet agency mission needs yet protect free speech and freedom of expression, as well as the artistic license of the creator of the work.

