31.201-4 Determining allocability

L0:A cost is allocable to a Government contract if it—
L1:(a) Is assignable or chargeable to one or more cost objectives on the basis of relative benefits received or other equitable relationship;
L1:(b) Is incurred specifically for the contract;
L1:(c) Benefits both the contract and other work, and can be distributed to them in reasonable proportion to the benefits received; or
L1:(d) Is necessary to the overall operation of the business, although a direct relationship to any particular cost objective cannot be shown.

32.000 Scope of part

L0:This part addresses policies and procedures for contract financing, funding and other payment matters. It implements 10 U.S.C. Chapter 277, 41 U.S.C. Chapter 45, and 50 U.S.C. Chapter 55, which authorize contract financing guarantees. This part addresses—
L1:(a) Payment methods, including partial payments and progress payments based on percentage or stage of completion;
L1:(b) Loan guarantees, advance payments, and progress payments based on costs;
L1:(c) Administration of debts to the Government arising out of contracts;
L1:(d) Contract funding, including the use of contract clauses limiting costs or funds;
L1:(e) Assignment of claims to aid in private financing;
L1:(f) Selected payment clauses;
L1:(g) Financing of purchases of commercial products and commercial services;
L1:(h) Financing of other than commercial purchases;
L1:(i) Performance-based payments;
L1:(j) Electronic funds transfer payments; and
L1:(k) Fast payment procedures.

