L0:252.244-7001 Contractor Purchasing System Administration.
L0:Basic. As prescribed in 244.305-71 and 244.305-71 (a), use the following clause:
L0:CONTRACTOR PURCHASING SYSTEM ADMINISTRATION-BASIC (JAN 2025)
L1:(a) Definitions. As used in this clause—
L0:“Acceptable purchasing system” means a purchasing system that complies with the system criteria in paragraph (c) of this
L0:clause.
L0:[Material weakness means a deficiency or combination of deficiencies in the internal control over information in contractor
L0:business systems, such that there is a reasonable possibility that a material misstatement of such information will not be
L0:prevented, or detected and corrected, on a timely basis. A reasonable possibility exists when the likelihood of an event
L0:occurring is—
L1:(1) Probable; or
L1:(2) More than remote but less than likely (section 806 of Pub. L. 116-283).
L0:“Purchasing system” means the Contractor’s system or systems for purchasing and subcontracting, including make-or-buy
L0:decisions, the selection of vendors, analysis of quoted prices, negotiation of prices with vendors, placing and administering
L0:of orders, and expediting delivery of materials.
L1:(b) General. The Contractor shall establish and maintain an acceptable purchasing system. Failure to maintain an
L0:acceptable purchasing system, as defined in this clause, may result in disapproval of the system by the Contracting Officer
L0:and/or withholding of payments.
L1:(c) System criteria. The Contractor’s purchasing system shall—
L1:(1) Have an adequate system description including policies, procedures, and purchasing practices that comply with the
L0:Federal Acquisition Regulation (FAR) and the Defense Federal Acquisition Regulation Supplement (DFARS);
L1:(2) Ensure that all applicable purchase orders and subcontracts contain all flowdown clauses, including terms and
L0:conditions and any other clauses needed to carry out the requirements of the prime contract;
L1:(3) Maintain an organization plan that establishes clear lines of authority and responsibility;
L1:(4) Ensure all purchase orders are based on authorized requisitions and include a complete and accurate history of purchase
L0:transactions to support vendor selected, price paid, and document the subcontract/purchase order files which are subject to
L0:Government review;
L1:(5) Establish and maintain adequate documentation to provide a complete and accurate history of purchase transactions to
L0:support vendors selected and prices paid;
L1:(6) Apply a consistent make-or-buy policy that is in the best interest of the Government;
L1:(7) Use competitive sourcing to the maximum extent practicable, and ensure debarred or suspended contractors are
L0:properly excluded from contract award;
L1:(8) Evaluate price, quality, delivery, technical capabilities, and financial capabilities of competing vendors to ensure fair
L0:and reasonable prices;
L1:(9) Require management level justification and adequate cost or price analysis, as applicable, for any sole or single source
L0:award;
L1:(10) Perform timely and adequate cost or price analysis and technical evaluation for each subcontractor and supplier
L0:proposal or quote to ensure fair and reasonable subcontract prices;
L1:(11) Document negotiations in accordance with FAR 15.406-3;
L1:(12) Seek, take, and document economically feasible purchase discounts, including cash discounts, trade discounts,
L0:quantity discounts, rebates, freight allowances, and company-wide volume discounts;
L1:(13) Ensure proper type of contract selection and prohibit issuance of cost-plus-a-percentage-of-cost subcontracts;
